    "n_params": 3,
    "rationale": "The quadratic x^2 term in the incumbent is odd in x and contributes almost nothing (NMSE 0.09694 -> 0.09639), because the measured x-bin mean residuals are all small (~0.0006 to 0.0028) with no monotone curvature pattern. A symmetric cubic term x^3 is more physically plausible for an oscillator whose restoring force softens/hardens at larger amplitude, is odd (consistent with a=-kx structure), and shares the same parameter count. I keep p0*x + p1*v and replace x^2 with x^3. I claim the incumbent's x-bin mean residuals are all small (below 0.003) and that its total bias is tiny relative to MSE. I predict only a small NMSE decrease: the high-v bin rmse (0.032) hints at amplitude-dependent structure, but the binned evidence is association only, so the cubic may absorb little. I expect at most a modest improvement, not a large drop.",
